.TH HOSTS 5
.SH NAME
hosts \- static IPv4 host database
.SH DESCRIPTION
/etc/hosts contains an IPv4 address, canonical name and up to 35 aliases,
separated by spaces or tabs. Comments begin with #. Names and aliases match
without regard to ASCII case. Invalid addresses, malformed records and lines
longer than 1023 bytes are skipped completely. The default file maps
127.0.0.1 to localhost.
.PP
gethostent iterates entries using static storage overwritten on the next call.
sethostent rewinds and optionally keeps the stream open across lookups;
endhostent closes it. These interfaces are not reentrant.
